	"notes": "This skincare shop's homepage is built as a stack of full-width bands, and none of them are capped to a centred measure — the page uses the entire width of the browser at every size, from a phone up to an ultrawide monitor. The big opening band is a headline and button sitting on top of one enormous bleeding photo, not a real side-by-side split. Further down, a row of nine photo cards scrolls sideways for a social-media feed, and an odd thing happens there: instead of fitting more cards on a wider screen the way a normal card wall would, EACH card just gets wider — 224px on a laptop, almost 700px on an ultrawide. The footer is the one place this page uses a real grid: four even columns of links. A cookie consent popup covers most of the opening band in every screenshot this tool took, which matters for how this record was written — the real design of that band came mostly from the CSS scan, not from what the pictures could show.",
